    !> ``lower``, the first i
    !> elements of the Householder vector \f$v_{l_i}\f$ are zero, and \f$v_{l_i}[i+1] = 1\f$. If
    !> ``uplo`` indicates ``upper``,
    !> the last n-i elements of the Householder vector \f$v_{l_i}\f$ are zero, and \f$v_{l_i}[i] =
    !> 1\f$.
    !>
    !> @param[in]
